Minato's patch to frameworks/base's core/java/android/view/accessibility/AccessibilityNodeInfo.java at android-15.0.0_r1
(Apache-2.0), services batch D: no direct accessibility connection.

Why: setQueryFromAppProcessEnabled links a node to the view root's direct connection, and usingDirectConnection asks
AccessibilityInteractionClient whether a connection is a DirectAccessibilityConnection, which needs the interaction
connection's AIDL and a service that answers. Minato has no accessibility service (ADR-0041), so no connection to the
window exists: the node stays unlinked, which is what an app's node is on Android without a service, and no connection
is a direct one. Every query over a connection then answers as Android does for a node without one (null, false or an
empty list), through framework/java/android/view/accessibility/AccessibilityInteractionClient.java.

tools/build-framework.sh applies it to a copy in build/framework/src, never to build/sources.

--- a/core/java/android/view/accessibility/AccessibilityNodeInfo.java
+++ b/core/java/android/view/accessibility/AccessibilityNodeInfo.java
@@ -4056,7 +4056,8 @@
             throw new IllegalStateException(
                     "Cannot link a node to a view that is not attached to a window.");
         }
-        setConnectionId(viewRootImpl.getDirectAccessibilityConnectionId());
+        // Minato has no direct connection: a node stays unlinked, as an app's node is without a service.
+        setConnectionId(UNDEFINED_CONNECTION_ID);
     }
 
     /**
@@ -4084,8 +4085,7 @@
     }
 
     private static boolean usingDirectConnection(int connectionId) {
-        return AccessibilityInteractionClient.getConnection(
-                connectionId) instanceof DirectAccessibilityConnection;
+        return false;
     }
 
